    "finding": "The strict default-five-worker linkcheck varied sharply: PR #3068 took about 375 seconds with seven rate-limit waits across five existing GitHub URLs, while exact main took about 72 seconds with one wait. Both strict builds succeeded. The paired outcome shows intermittent 429 latency but does not isolate worker count; candidate and main validate distinct source states. A bounded worker-count experiment remains justified.",
